 /// True when `span` is exactly one `case … end` (its `case` closes at the last token).
+
+/// `sum(bal * calculated rw)` where `rw` is an earlier NON-aggregate SELECT item
+/// (a CASE or an arithmetic expression): the aggregate folds per source row, where
+/// no output alias is bound, so the reference resolved to a missing column and
+/// the whole aggregate silently came out missing (BUG-sqlaggcalcarg). SAS
+/// evaluates the alias's expression per row inside the fold. Inline the item's
+/// tokens in place of `calculated <alias>` — `( expr )` for an expression item,
+/// `case … end` for a CASE item — so computeAggExpr sees a self-contained
+/// argument. A reference to an AGGREGATE alias is inlined as its `agg(…)` call so
+/// computeAggExpr's nested-summary check reports it the way SAS does.
+fn inlineCalculatedInAggArgs(arena: std.mem.Allocator, items: []Item) !void {
